{
 "plan": {
  "title": "Household Survey Coverage & Activity",
  "subtitle": "Monitoring survey reach across villages and enumerators with submission trends",
  "panels": [
   {
    "id": "p1",
    "kind": "kpi",
    "title": "Total Households Surveyed",
    "sql": "SELECT COUNT(*) AS n FROM \"household_survey\"",
    "unit": ""
   },
   {
    "id": "p2",
    "kind": "kpi",
    "title": "Active Villages",
    "sql": "SELECT COUNT(DISTINCT \"village\") AS n FROM \"household_survey\" WHERE \"village\" IS NOT NULL",
    "unit": ""
   },
   {
    "id": "p3",
    "kind": "kpi",
    "title": "Active Enumerators",
    "sql": "SELECT COUNT(DISTINCT \"enumerator_name\") AS n FROM \"household_survey\" WHERE \"enumerator_name\" IS NOT NULL",
    "unit": ""
   },
   {
    "id": "p4",
    "kind": "bar",
    "title": "Coverage by Village (Top 15)",
    "sql": "SELECT \"village\", COUNT(*) AS count FROM \"household_survey\" WHERE \"village\" IS NOT NULL GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 2 DESC LIMIT 15",
    "x": "village",
    "y": [
     "count"
    ]
   },
   {
    "id": "p5",
    "kind": "bar",
    "title": "Coverage by Enumerator",
    "sql": "SELECT \"enumerator_name\", COUNT(*) AS count FROM \"household_survey\" WHERE \"enumerator_name\" IS NOT NULL GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 2 DESC",
    "x": "enumerator_name",
    "y": [
     "count"
    ]
   },
   {
    "id": "p6",
    "kind": "line",
    "title": "Daily Submissions Trend",
    "sql": "SELECT DATE(\"_submission_time\") AS day, COUNT(*) AS count FROM \"household_survey\" WHERE \"_submission_time\" IS NOT NULL GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 1",
    "x": "day",
    "y": [
     "count"
    ]
   },
   {
    "id": "p7",
    "kind": "table",
    "title": "Village Coverage Details",
    "sql": "SELECT \"village\", COUNT(*) AS total_households, COUNT(DISTINCT \"enumerator_name\") AS unique_enumerators FROM \"household_survey\" WHERE \"village\" IS NOT NULL GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 2 DESC LIMIT 20"
   }
  ],
  "narrative": "The survey has covered {{p1}} households across {{p2}} villages, with data collected by {{p3}} enumerators. \n\nCoverage is not uniform; the top village accounts for {{p4[0]}} households, while the least covered among the top 15 has {{p4[14]}}. \n\nEnumerator workload varies significantly, with the most active enumerator handling {{p5[0]}} households compared to {{p5[9]}} for the least active. \n\nSubmission activity shows a trend over time, with the highest daily volume reaching {{p6[0]}} households on a single day."
 },
